&lt;h2 id="garden-description"&gt;Garden Description&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;!-- This is the main text describing the garden --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Discovered during excavation of Boulevard Gambetta, this house, in its original phase, had a central room with a painted décor of dolphins and aquatic motifs. In a second phase, towards the middle of the second century, this room [1] was transformed into a light well. It was a court open to the sky, though somewhat protected by the projection of a roof. One band of the former floor was kept; all the rest was covered by hauled-in earth, perhaps for planting. In the northwest corner of the court were found two vats for crushing lime.&lt;/p&gt;
